{# The hop from this site to the bank's payment page.

   This is deliberately a page and not a 302. ZarinPal matches the HTTP
   `Referer` of the request that lands on StartPay against the domain
   registered for the gateway, and shows the payer a "you are leaving an
   unknown site" interstitial when it does not match. A 302 sends no `Referer`
   of its own — the browser forwards whatever referrer the request to /pay/{id}
   carried, which for a link opened from an email, an app or a chat is nothing
   at all. A navigation started by script on this page does send one, and it is
   this domain.

   So the redirect has to happen in the browser, from a document served by us.
   Please do not turn it back into a 302.

   Everything here is inline and the navigation is started from <head>, before
   the body is parsed: it costs one small document and no extra requests, and
   the payer never sees the markup below. It exists for the seconds before the
   bank answers, and for browsers with scripting turned off. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ locale.value }}" dir="{{ direction }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
{# Sent before the navigation is started so it applies to it. `origin` gives
   ZarinPal the scheme and host it needs to match and nothing else — never the
   payment id in our path. The browser default would do the same, but this page
   cannot afford to inherit a stricter policy set somewhere upstream. #}
<meta name="referrer" content="origin">
<script>window.location.replace("{{ redirectUrl|e('js') }}");</script>
<noscript><meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ redirectUrl }}"></noscript>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<title>{{ t('checkout.redirecting_title') }}</title>
<link rel="icon" href="data:,">
<style>
    body { margin: 0; display: flex; min-height: 100vh; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
           font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; background: #f5f6f8; color: #1f2430; }
    .bounce { max-width: 24rem; padding: 2rem; text-align: center; }
    .bounce p { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.8; }
    .bounce a { display: inline-block; padding: .6rem 1.4rem; border-radius: .4rem;
                background: #1f2430; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="bounce">
    <p>{{ t('checkout.redirecting_body') }}</p>
    {# Also the manual escape hatch when the script above is blocked: a click on
       a same-document link carries the referrer just as the script does. #}
    <a href="{{ redirectUrl }}">{{ t('checkout.redirecting_manual') }}</a>
</div>
</body>
</html>
